---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { firm } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { text: 'Scope of this policy', slug: 'scope-of-this-policy' },
  { text: 'Information we collect', slug: 'information-we-collect' },
  { text: 'How we use information', slug: 'how-we-use-information' },
  { text: 'When we share information', slug: 'when-we-share-information' },
  { text: 'Cookies and analytics', slug: 'cookies-and-analytics' },
  { text: 'How long we keep information', slug: 'how-long-we-keep-information' },
  { text: 'Security', slug: 'security' },
  { text: 'Your California privacy rights', slug: 'your-california-privacy-rights' },
  { text: 'Children', slug: 'children' },
  { text: 'Changes to this policy', slug: 'changes-to-this-policy' },
  { text: 'How to contact us', slug: 'how-to-contact-us' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Sulfab Law Office P.C."
  description="How Sulfab Law Office P.C. collects, uses, and protects information submitted through sulfablaw.com, and the privacy rights available to California residents."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  lede="How Sulfab Law Office P.C. collects, uses, and safeguards information submitted through this website."
  updated="2026-11-21"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    Sulfab Law Office P.C. (“the firm,” “we,” “us”) respects the privacy of visitors to
    <a href="https://www.sulfablaw.com">sulfablaw.com</a> and of the people who contact us about
    immigration matters. This policy explains what information we collect through the website, why
    we collect it, how it is used, and the choices available to you. It applies to this website only.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scope-of-this-policy">Scope of this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers information submitted through the website’s contact and consultation forms,
    by email, or by telephone in response to the website. It does not describe the confidentiality
    obligations that apply once the firm is formally retained. Communications with the firm are
    protected by the attorney-client privilege only after an engagement is established; see our
    <a href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a current client, the engagement agreement and applicable rules of professional
    conduct govern how your case information is handled, and they control if they differ from this
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information you choose to give us, plus limited technical information.</p>
  <h3>Information you provide</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Name, email address, and telephone number.</li>
    <li>
      The content of your message, including any details about your immigration status, case,
      deadlines, detention, or family members that you choose to include.
    </li>
    <li>
      The case type you select in a consultation form (for example, asylum, removal defense,
      detention, or a family petition).
    </li>
    <li>Any documents you send by email or bring to a consultation.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Browser type, device type, and operating system.</li>
    <li>The pages you visit on this website and the page that referred you.</li>
    <li>Approximate location derived from your IP address, at the city or region level.</li>
    <li>Date and time of your visit.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not send Social Security numbers, passport copies, or other sensitive documents
    through the website forms. We will tell you how to transmit records securely once we begin
    working together.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-information">How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your inquiry and schedule a consultation.</li>
    <li>To evaluate whether the firm can help with your matter and to identify conflicts of interest.</li>
    <li>To communicate with you about your inquiry or case.</li>
    <li>To operate, maintain, and improve the website and its content.</li>
    <li>To protect the website against spam, abuse, and security threats.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal and professional obligations, including recordkeeping rules.</li>
    <li>
      To send occasional updates about the firm or its services, only where permitted and with an
      option to opt out.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use the information you submit to make automated decisions that produce legal or
    similarly significant effects, and we do not sell your personal information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="when-we-share-information">When we share information</h2>
  <p>
    We share information only as needed to operate the firm and this website, or as the law
    requires. That includes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers.</strong> Website hosting, email, scheduling, and analytics vendors
      that process information on our behalf under confidentiality obligations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Professional advisers.</strong> Accountants, insurers, and ethics counsel where
      necessary for the firm’s operations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal requirements.</strong> Courts, regulators, or other parties when required by
      law, subpoena, or the rules of professional conduct.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Protection of rights.</strong> Where necessary to investigate fraud, protect the
      website, or defend the firm’s legal rights.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business changes.</strong> In connection with a merger, acquisition, or transfer of
      the practice, subject to continued confidentiality.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell or rent personal information to third parties for their own marketing.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies-and-analytics">Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website may use cookies and similar technologies to remember preferences and to understand
    how visitors use the site. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; some parts
    of the site may not work as intended if you do. If we add third-party analytics or advertising
    tools that collect personal information, we will update this policy and, where required, request
    consent first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-long-we-keep-information">How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep inquiry information for as long as needed to respond, evaluate the matter, and meet
    recordkeeping obligations, then delete or anonymize it. If you become a client, your file is
    retained according to the firm’s records policy and the applicable rules of professional
    conduct, which may require retention for several years after a matter closes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect
    information submitted through this website. No method of transmission or storage is completely
    secure, however, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. If you believe information you sent
    us has been compromised, contact us immediately using the details below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-california-privacy-rights">Your California privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    California residents may have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by
    the California Privacy Rights Act. Subject to applicable exceptions, these include the right to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Know what categories of personal information we collect, use, and disclose.</li>
    <li>Request access to the specific personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate personal information.</li>
    <li>Request deletion of personal information, subject to legal retention obligations.</li>
    <li>Opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information — we do not sell or share it.</li>
    <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising these rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make a request, contact us using the details below. We will verify your identity before
    acting, and we may need to keep certain records where the law or professional rules require it.
    An authorized agent may submit a request on your behalf with written permission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is intended for adults. It is not directed to children under 13, and we do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children through the site. If you believe a child
    has submitted information, contact us and we will delete it. Information about a child’s
    immigration matter should be provided by a parent or guardian through a secure channel.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes-to-this-policy">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the website or the law changes. The “last updated” date at the top
    of the page shows when it was revised. Material changes will be reflected here, and continued
    use of the website after an update means you accept the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-to-contact-us">How to contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or a privacy request can be sent to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sulfab Law Office P.C.</strong></li>
    <li>{firm.address.street}, {firm.address.city}, {firm.address.state} {firm.address.zip}</li>
    <li>Email: <a href={firm.emailHref}>{firm.email}</a></li>
    <li>Telephone: <a href={firm.phoneHref}>{firm.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This policy is provided for transparency and does not create rights beyond those available under
    applicable law. It should be reviewed by the firm’s counsel before publication if the firm’s data
    practices change.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
